// fileio_stdio.rho — Phase 10 canonical example
//
// Echo stdin lines to stdout, one line at a time, terminating on
// end-of-input.  Uses the standard `readLine()` → CharStream →
// `writeLine(charStream)` composition: each read produces a bounded
// CharStream (single line up to LF or EOS), and each write drains
// that CharStream and appends the newline.
//
// Sequence:
//   1. Look up Fs and resolve `stdin`, `stdout` caps.
//   2. Tail-recursive loop `echoLoop`:
//        - `stdin!readLine()` → `[true, lineStream]` or
//          `[false, "EOS", _]` on end-of-input.
//        - `stdout!writeLine(lineStream)` drains the CharStream and
//          appends LF to stdout.
//        - Recur.
//        - On EOS, terminate the loop.
//
// Concurrency note (Phase 8): `stdin!readLine()` acquires a per-
// stdin sequential lock for the outer stream's lifetime.  A second
// `stdin!readLine()` while a prior CharStream is still live blocks
// on that lock (FSERR_BUSY under wait:false; blocks under wait:true).
// The echo loop respects this by draining each CharStream fully
// before starting the next readLine.
//
// ## Prerequisite: stdio replay wiring
//
// Stdio input capture / follower replay for Stdin.fsRead was
// deferred from Phase 6 to Phase 10 (see implementation-plan.md
// line 332).  This example runs cleanly on a lead node with a
// live stdin fd but does NOT yet produce deterministic replay
// records — a follower would re-read from its own (typically
// empty) stdin.  Slice 10c wires the capture side.
//
// Companion regression: casper/tests/genesis/contracts/
// fileio_examples_spec.rs :: fileio_stdio_caps_are_resolvable
// (verifies Fs.stdin / Fs.stdout return usable caps; the full
// echo-loop test lands with slice 10c's replay wiring).

new
  rl(`rho:registry:lookup`),
  fsCh,
  echoLoop
in {
  rl!(`rho:id:zphjgsfy13h1k85isc8rtwtgt3t9zzt5pjd5ihykfmyapfc4wt3x5h`, *fsCh) |
  for(@(_, fs) <- fsCh) {
    for(@[true, stdin]  <- @fs!?("stdin");
        @[true, stdout] <- @fs!?("stdout")) {
      contract echoLoop(done) = {
        for(@r <- @stdin!?("readLine")) {
          match r {
            [true, lineStream] => {
              for(@wr <- @stdout!?("writeLine", lineStream)) {
                match wr {
                  [true] => echoLoop!(*done)
                  _      => done!(("writeLine failed", wr))
                }
              }
            }
            // Note: per FIP §930 / §1090 the current `Stdin.readLine`
            // contract always replies `[true, streamHandle]` — EOS is
            // observed by draining the returned CharStream, not at the
            // outer readLine call.  A pre-EOF `readLine` returns a
            // stream whose first `next()` yields `[false, "EOS", _]`.
            // This outer `[false, "EOS", _]` arm is defensive against
            // a hypothetical alternative Stdin variant that fires EOS
            // at the outer call; the current implementation will
            // instead fall through to the write-loop below and observe
            // EOS through `writeLine`'s drain.  Slice 10c restructures
            // this example to observe EOS through the drain and lands
            // the full echo-loop E2E test.
            [false, "EOS", _] => done!(("done, EOS", true))
            _                 => done!(("readLine failed", r))
          }
        }
      } |
      new done in {
        echoLoop!(*done) |
        for(@_ <- done) { Nil }
      }
    }
  }
}
